      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p>This policy explains the types of information ClassicFin Hub may handle across appointment requests, tenant setup, staff access, customer records, transactions, reports, billing, and support.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="legal-grid reveal">
      <aside class="legal-aside">
        <a href="/#book">Book a platform demo</a>
        <a href="/signin">Sign in to dashboard</a>
        <a href="/pricing">View pricing</a>
        <a href="/price-compare">Compare plan prices</a>
        <a href="tel:211921789914">Call +211 921 789 914</a>
        <a href="https://api.whatsapp.com/send?phone=211921789914">WhatsApp support</a>
        <a href="mailto:info@classicfinhub.com">Email ClassicFin Hub</a>
      </aside>
      <article class="legal-content">
<h2>Information we collect</h2><p>We may collect appointment details, business owner contacts, tenant profile data, staff profile data, customer profile data, KYC fields when configured, branch data, transaction records, receipts, reports, billing records, support messages, device/session details, and audit logs.</p>
<h2>How information is used</h2><p>Information is used to create tenants, invite owners and staff, operate enabled modules, generate receipts and reports, send notifications, manage billing, enforce permissions, support customers, audit sensitive actions, and improve platform reliability.</p>
<h2>Tenant isolation</h2><p>The blueprint is based on database-per-tenant separation. Tenant users and operations are stored in the tenant database, tenant files use tenant-specific storage paths, and cache keys are tenant-prefixed.</p>
<h2>Security expectations</h2><p>Passwords and transfer PINs should be hashed. Sensitive actions should be audited. Tenants should not send passwords, PINs, API keys, or private credentials through public forms or chats.</p>
<h2>Your choices</h2><p>Contact the platform team to ask about submitted information, support records, tenant profile corrections, or account access concerns where appropriate.</p>
      </article>
    </section>
